# Git version tag

When the user asks you to create a git commit:

1. Read `APP_VERSION_A` from `src/appinfo.h` (the string inside `"..."`).
2. After the commit succeeds, create an annotated tag `v{version}` on that commit, e.g. `v0.3.1`.
3. If the tag already exists locally, move it to the new commit (`git tag -f`).
4. Do not push the tag (or any remote) unless the user explicitly asks.

Example:

```bash
VER=$(grep -oP '#define APP_VERSION_A\s+"\K[^"]+' src/appinfo.h)
git tag -f -a "v$VER" -m "v$VER"
```
